    "id": "2101990070152581315",
    "text": "Your Posture Needs Work\u203c\ufe0f\n\nThese 5 resistance-band exercises target the muscles that help keep your shoulders and shoulder blades organized:\n\n\u2022 Rhomboids + mid/lower traps \u2022 Rear delts \u2022 Lats \u2022 Scapular stabilizers \u2022 Upper-back endurance\n\u2714\ufe0f Targets The Rhomboids & Mid/Lower Traps To Help Pull Your Shoulders Back\n\u2714\ufe0f Strengthens The Rear Delts To Build Better Balance Around The Shoulder Joint\n\u2714\ufe0f Activates The Lats & Improves Your Pulling Strength Without Heavy Weights\n\u2714\ufe0f Trains The Smaller Stabilizing Muscles That Control Your Shoulder Blades\n\n\u2714\ufe0f Builds Upper-Back Endurance To Help You Maintain Better Posture Throughout The Day\n\nHours of sitting, driving, and looking down at your phone can leave your chest feeling tight while your upper back does less work than it should.\n\nThat\u2019s where these movements come in.\n\nThe goal isn't to force your shoulders backward all day.\n\nIt\u2019s to build a back strong enough to support better positioning without constant effort.\n\nKeep the reps slow. Control the band. Let the back\u2014not the arms\u2014do the work.\n\nYou don't need massive weights.\n\nYou need tension, control, and consistency.",
    "raw_text": {
      "text": "Your Posture Needs Work\u203c\ufe0f\n\nThese 5 resistance-band exercises target the muscles that help keep your shoulders and shoulder blades organized:\n\n\u2022 Rhomboids + mid/lower traps \u2022 Rear delts \u2022 Lats \u2022 Scapular stabilizers \u2022 Upper-back endurance\n\u2714\ufe0f Targets The Rhomboids & Mid/Lower Traps To Help Pull Your Shoulders Back\n\u2714\ufe0f Strengthens The Rear Delts To Build Better Balance Around The Shoulder Joint\n\u2714\ufe0f Activates The Lats & Improves Your Pulling Strength Without Heavy Weights\n\u2714\ufe0f Trains The Smaller Stabilizing Muscles That Control Your Shoulder Blades\n\n\u2714\ufe0f Builds Upper-Back Endurance To Help You Maintain Better Posture Throughout The Day\n\nHours of sitting, driving, and looking down at your phone can leave your chest feeling tight while your upper back does less work than it should.\n\nThat\u2019s where these movements come in.\n\nThe goal isn't to force your shoulders backward all day.\n\nIt\u2019s to build a back strong enough to support better positioning without constant effort.\n\nKeep the reps slow. Control the band. Let the back\u2014not the arms\u2014do the work.\n\nYou don't need massive weights.\n\nYou need tension, control, and consistency.",
